Proposed change (not applied): NativeUfs serves NativeRamBlock's persistent store from the iOS Data file in Android's /data
(../PaganiPersistentData/DataFileUfs.h) when built with -DNATIVE_UFS_DATA_FILE=1 and booted with pagani-data-file=1|2.
- RootCommands.h: hostInWindow also accepts DataFileUfs.h's verified data blocks (and the one REVOKED slot block while XNU revokes);
  the read-only command filter lets WRITE(10)/SYNCHRONIZE CACHE(10) through only while dataFileWritesArmed(); hostSyncCache likewise.
  Without NATIVE_UFS_DATA_FILE (and in probe-only builds) the file is unchanged in effect.
- NativeUfs.cpp: includes the glue inside the transport namespace, records the lowest root window offset, routes
  native_ufs_store_mode/open/read/write/sync to it while pagani-data-file is set, exports native_data_file_diag() for the boot page.
Build: keep -DNATIVE_UFS_READ_ONLY=1, add -DNATIVE_UFS_DATA_FILE=1; PaganiPersistentData/ must sit next to NativeUfs/.
Check: cd UniXNU-Pagani-Drivers && git apply --check drivers/PaganiPersistentData/integration/NativeUfs.patch

